Language English
Debug Off

Book Driveway Ordered No Keep Looped
	
	Page Place 
		Triggered By @ExploreDrivewayViaStartup
		
		Add TileDriveway

		Text """
			It's 3:00 and you're on time. The man your  
			friend spoke with on the phone---Benjamin---  
			should be here to meet you.  

			As you walk up the driveway, you see how  
			poorly maintained the house and grounds are.  
			The drive is paved, but cracked and pocked.  
			Weeds grow waist-high on either side, and you  
			wonder what might be hiding there.  

			Place the {c:TileDriveway} tile as indicated.  
		"""
		
	End Page Place

	Page PlaceInvestigators
		Add TokenDrivewayInvestigators
		
		Text """
			You wonder what you were thinking when you  
			said <<yes>> to your friend. Place your  
			investigators as indicated.  
		"""
		
		Remove TokenDrivewayInvestigators
	End Page PlaceInvestigators

	Page PlaceExploreKitchenViaDriveway
		Add TokenExploreKitchenViaDriveway!

		Text """
			After circling the house, you are not  
			surprised to find the door beside you covered  
			in mud and spiderwebs. Like the rest of the  
			house, the paint is peeling and the wood  
			shows signs of dry rot.  

			Place an Explore token as indicated.  
		"""

	End Page PlaceExploreKitchenViaDriveway

	Page PlaceGate
		Add TokenExploreBackyardViaDrivewayBlocked!
		
		Text """
			At the end of the drive stands a gate that  
			leads around to the back of the house. Place  
			an Explore token as indicated.  
		"""
	End Page PlaceGate

	Page PlaceGardenTool
		Add TokenSearchDrivewayGardenTool!

		Text """
			The weeds behind the house are even taller  
			than those in front. Near the corner of the  
			drive, something hidden beneath them catches  
			your eye. Place a Search token as indicated.  
		"""
		
		initialized = true
	End Page PlaceGardenTool

	Page PlaceWendy
		Visible If #HeroWendyAdams
		
		Text QItemWendyGun """
			As she walks up the drive, Wendy Adams trips  
			and falls. She twists her ankle and skins her  
			knees. When she looks up, she spots  
			something in the weeds. Wendy gains the  
			{c:QItemWendyGun} Common Item.  

			When she finally stands, she does not feel as  
			agile as usual. In this scenario, Wendy can  
			become Restrained.  
		"""
	End Page PlaceWendy

	Page EndPlace 
		No Text
		Exit
	End Page EndPlace

	Page SearchGardenTool
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchDrivewayGardenTool
		
		Prolog """
			The weeds along the edge of the driveway are  
			tall, thick, and long dead. Whatever lies  
			beneath them has been tightly bound for  
			years.  
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchDrivewayGardenTool

		Text QItemGardenTool """
			You rummage through the weeds and uncover  
			something useful. Gain the  
			{c:QItemGardenTool} Common Item, then  
			discard this Search token.  

			As you pull it free, a child's doll is  
			exposed. Its clothing is ragged and the paint  
			is chipped. You think of the children found  
			here and wonder if it once belonged to one  
			of them.  

			Gain 1 {clue}, then suffer 1 facedown Horror  
			({will} negates).  
		"""
		
		foundGardenTool = true		
		Exit
	End Page SearchGardenTool

	Page SearchJournal
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchOutsideJournal
		
		Prolog "Benjamin dropped a book here."
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchDrivewayJournal

		Text QItemJournal """
			Up close, you see that it is thin and  
			leather-bound. You pick it up and flip  
			through the pages---it's a journal. The  
			first entry was scrawled last Sunday. You  
			should return it to Benjamin, but perhaps  
			you can glance through it first.  

			Gain the {c:QItemJournal} Unique Item, then  
			discard this Search token. An investigator  
			holding the {c:QItemJournal} can interact  
			with it in the app.  
		"""
		
		foundJournal = true
		Exit
	End Page SearchJournal	

	Page ExploreBackyardViaDriveway
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreBackyardViaDrivewayBlocked
		
		Text """
			An intricate wrought-iron gate is set into  
			a stone wall. Like the rest of the house,  
			the paint peels and the bars are rusted.  
			The gate looks as though it was once  
			exceptionally strong, but perhaps not now.  

			It likely would not take much effort to  
			push it open ({strength}).  
		"""
		
		Test Quota 3 Set exploredBackyardNotNicely
		
		If exploredBackyardNotNicely Then Goto ExploreNotNice
		Goto ExploreNice
	End Page ExploreBackyardViaDriveway

	Page ExploreNotNice
		Not Visible
		Add TokenDriveWayBen!
		Remove TokenExploreBackyardViaDrivewayBlocked

		Text """
			You give it everything you've got---and the  
			gate, rusty and poorly maintained, gives  
			way with a terrible crash. As the noise  
			echoes down the drive, an angry man storms  
			around the corner and strides up behind you.  

			Place the Purple Man token as indicated;  
			this is Benjamin Smythe, the man your  
			friend spoke with on the phone.  

			Discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		exploredBackyardNicely = false
		Goto ExploreNotNiceBen
	End Page ExploreNotNice

	Page ExploreNotNiceBen
		Not Visible
		Text """
			As you turn to face Benjamin, you hear a  
			second crash beyond the gate.  

			<<What are you doing?! I just had that  
			rehung yesterday!>> he yells. <<I hired  
			you to help get this house ready for sale,  
			not destroy it. You were to meet me here;  
			I'm not sure why you thought it wise to  
			start without me.>>  

			Benjamin brushes past you with a harrumph.  
			Discard the Purple Man token.  

			You've only just arrived, and the client is  
			already furious. This could end badly for  
			you and your friend's business.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenDrivewayBen
		Goto ExploreNotNiceJournal
	End Page ExploreNotNiceBen

	Page ExploreNotNiceJournal
		Not Visible
		Add TokenSearchDrivewayJournal!, TokenExploreBackyardViaDriveway!
		
		Text """
			You look down and shake your head. As you  
			do, you notice a book lying where Benjamin  
			had been standing. Place a Search token  
			as indicated.  

			You turn back toward the gate, take a  
			steadying breath, and...  

			Place a Sight token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page ExploreNotNiceJournal

	Page ExploreNice
		Remove TokenExploreBackyardViaDrivewayBlocked
		Add TokenDrivewayBen!

		Text """
			You gently pull the gate, and it opens  
			with surprising ease. Now that you look  
			closer, you see someone recently cleaned  
			the hinges and oiled them. You are glad  
			you did not force it. Discard this  
			Explore token.  

			<<I see the handyman fixed the gate  
			yesterday. That will make things easier.>>  
			You start, not having heard the man walk  
			up behind you.  

			Place the Purple Man token as indicated.
		"""
		
		exploredBackyardNicely = true
		Goto ExploreNiceBen
	End Page ExploreNice

	Page ExploreNiceBen
		Text """
			You meet the eyes of an aging but vigorous  
			man. He introduces himself as Benjamin  
			Smythe, the man your friend spoke with.  
			<<You'll want to follow me so we can get  
			started.>>  

			Benjamin turns and walks through the  
			now-open gate.  

			Discard the Purple Man token.
		"""

		Remove TokenDrivewayBen
		Goto ExploreNiceJournal
	End Page ExploreNiceBen

	Page ExploreNiceJournal
		Add TokenSearchDrivewayJournal!, TokenExploreBackyardViaDriveway!

		Text """
			You glance back and notice a book Benjamin  
			dropped. Place a Search token as indicated.  

			A moment later, you hear Benjamin yelp,  
			followed by a loud crash. You quickly turn  
			toward the gate. Place a Sight token as  
			indicated.
		"""

		Exit
	End Page ExploreNiceJournal
End Book Driveway